# Vercel auto-detects any top-level api/ directory as Vercel
# Serverless Functions. Our api/ folder is the FastAPI app deployed
# separately on Render — it was never meant to run on Vercel, and
# without this, Vercel builds a Python environment from
# api/requirements.txt on every deploy for no reason (confirmed in a
# real build log: "Installing required dependencies from
# api/requirements.txt..." when only the static frontend should be
# built here).
#
# CRITICAL: these patterns are anchored with a leading slash. An
# earlier unanchored version ("api/", no leading slash) matched ANY
# directory named "api" anywhere in the repo — including
# src/api/, the frontend's own API client folder (client.js), which is
# genuinely required by App.jsx and every chart component. That bug
# silently broke every production deploy with an unresolvable-import
# build failure, and cost a long, confusing debugging session before
# being traced back here — verified definitively with `git
# check-ignore`, not assumed: the unanchored pattern provably matched
# src/api/client.js; the anchored version below provably does not.
/api/
/pipeline/